[151.833772, "o", "1:## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment\r\n5:Mid-year QA found compliance holds disappearing after date corrections. This\r\n6:amendment supersedes any earlier wording about hold timing. For `compliance_hold`\r\n9:in effect after ledger load, meeting amendments, and compliance mail merges, but\r\n11:mail-driven status changes; this amendment governs only the hold flag.\r\n13:## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment — field notes\r\n31:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n33:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n41:Memo WP-2693 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagree"]
[151.833885, "o", "d on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n45:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n49:In July review, external advisors reviewed capital project capitalization and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n51:The committee packet references capital project capitalization as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n65:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archiv"]
